    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4450\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act granting retroactive tier IV membership in\nthe New York state and local employees' retirement system to Scott\nGoodfellow\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nScott Goodfellow was employed on December 27, 2009, by the county of\nSt. Lawrence Department of Corrections and filed retirement membership\napplications that day which should have given him Tier IV status.\nHowever, due to an administrative error the application was not\nprocessed until January 4, 2010, giving him Tier V status.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one allows Scott Goodfellow to become a member of the NY state\nand local employees' retirement system on December 27, 2009, if he\nfiles an application with the state Comptroller's office within one\nyear of this act becoming law. This will give him Tier 4 status in the\nNY state and local employees' retirement system.\n\nSection two provides that the county of St. Lawrence will pay for the\ncosts of implementing this bill. Section three is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAn administrative error should not strip Scott Goodfellow from his\nTier IV benefits.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016 - S. 6743 - Passed Senate/A. 9059a - Governmental Employees\nCommittee.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nScott Goodfellow is currently a Tier 5 member employed by the Power\nAuthority. If this legislation is enacted, there will be an\napproximate increase of $2,400 per year in the annual contributions by\nthe Power Authority. In future years, the cost will vary as the\nbilling rates and salaries of Scott Goodfellow change. In addition,\nthere will be a one-time past service cost of $2,300 to be paid by St.\nLawrence County.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
